msgid ""
"Use Boost_LIBRARIES instead of Boost_PYTHON_LIBRARY This was causing issues "
"when building with python3 since then ``Boost_PYTHON_LIBRARY`` is not set, "
"instead cmake sets ``Boost_PYTHON3_LIBRARY``. So instead of adding each "
"library separately, using ``Boost_LIBRARIES`` seems to be better. For "
"reference, from the cmake docs: ``` Boost_LIBRARIES        - Boost component "
"libraries to be linked Boost\\_<C>_LIBRARY      - Libraries to link for "
"component <C> ```"
msgstr ""

